    "title": "Deduplicate Prior Authorization Requests by Case",
    "prompt": "A `prior_auth_submissions` table tracks requests sent to insurance payers. Due to a system bug, some authorization cases were submitted multiple times with different `submission_id` values but identical `case_number`, `payer_id`, and `provider_npi`. For each duplicate set (same `case_number`, `payer_id`, `provider_npi`), keep only the submission with the lowest `submission_id` and delete all others. After deduplication, return all surviving rows ordered by `submission_id` ascending. The table uses `submission_id` as the primary key; duplicate keys are defined by the combination of `case_number`, `payer_id`, and `provider_npi`. Your solution must physically delete the duplicate rows and then show the final state of the table.",
